{
  "id": "25869_kakioeru",
  "headword": "{書|か}き{終|お}える",
  "reading": "かきおえる",
  "romaji": "kakioeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to finish writing",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to finish writing",
      "explanation": "To complete the act of writing something; to write to the end."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "25869_kakioeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "レポートを{書|か}き{終|お}えた。",
      "english": "I finished writing the report.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25869_kakioeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{手紙|てがみ}を{書|か}き{終|お}えてからポストに{入|い}れた。",
      "english": "I put it in the mailbox after finishing the letter.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25869_kakioeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{小説|しょうせつ}を{書|か}き{終|お}えるのに{三年|さんねん}かかった。",
      "english": "It took three years to finish writing the novel.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25869_kakioeru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{試験|しけん}{時間|じかん}の{終了|しゅうりょう}{直前|ちょくぜん}にやっと{全問|ぜんもん}{書|か}き{終|お}えることができた。",
      "english": "I was finally able to finish writing all the answers just before the exam time ran out.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound verb formed from {書|か}く (to write) + {終|お}える (to finish). The auxiliary verb {終|お}える attaches to the masu-stem of verbs to express completion of an action. This is one of the most common compound verb patterns in Japanese.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- レポートを{書|か}き{終|お}える: finish writing a report\n- {手紙|てがみ}を{書|か}き{終|お}える: finish writing a letter\n- {原稿|げんこう}を{書|か}き{終|お}える: finish writing a manuscript\n- {論文|ろんぶん}を{書|か}き{終|お}える: finish writing a thesis\n\nSIMILAR PATTERNS:\n- {読|よ}み{終|お}える: finish reading\n- {食|た}べ{終|お}える: finish eating\n- {飲|の}み{終|お}える: finish drinking\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {書|か}き{上|あ}げる: finish writing (with nuance of completing a major work)\n- {書|か}き{終|お}わる: finish writing (intransitive variant — the writing is finished)",
